          "text": "saṃcaraḥ | Tats_1.5 |",
          "segment_number": 78,
          "translated_text": "Evolution (<s>saṃcara</s>). | Tats_1.5 |"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "pratisaṃcaraḥ | Tats_1.6 |",
          "segment_number": 79,
          "translated_text": "Dissolution (<s>pratisaṃcara</s>). | Tats_1.6 |"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "adhyātmam | Tats_1.7 |",
          "segment_number": 80,
          "translated_text": "The subjective (<s>adhyātma</s>). | Tats_1.7 |"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "adhibhūtam | Tats_1.8 |",
          "segment_number": 81,
          "translated_text": "The objective (<s>adhibhūta</s>). | Tats_1.8 |"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "adhidaivatam | Tats_1.9 |",
          "segment_number": 82,
          "translated_text": "The divine (<s>adhidaivata</s>). | Tats_1.9 |"
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "2. Prakīrṇapādaḥ",
          "segment_number": 83,
          "translated_text": "2. <s>Prakīrṇapāda</s> (Miscellaneous Chapter)"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "pañcābhibuddhayaḥ | Tats_2.1 |",
          "segment_number": 84,
          "translated_text": "Five are the <s>abhibuddhis</s> (intellectual dispositions). | Tats_2.1 |"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "pañca karmayonayaḥ | Tats_2.2 |",
          "segment_number": 85,
          "translated_text": "Five are the <s>karmayonis</s> (sources of action). | Tats_2.2 |"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "pañca vāyavaḥ | Tats_2.3 |",
          "segment_number": 86,
          "translated_text": "Five are the <s>vāyus</s> (vital breaths). | Tats_2.3 |"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "pañca karmātmānaḥ | Tats_2.4 |",
          "segment_number": 87,
          "translated_text": "Five are the <s>karmātmans</s> (organs of action). | Tats_2.4 |"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "pañcaparvāvidyā | Tats_2.5 |",
          "segment_number": 88,
          "translated_text": "<s>Avidyā</s> (ignorance) has five divisions (<s>pañcaparva</s>). | Tats_2.5 |"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "aṣṭāviṃśatidhāśaktiḥ | Tats_2.6 |",
          "segment_number": 89,
          "translated_text": "<s>Aśakti</s> (incapacity) is of twenty-eight kinds. | Tats_2.6 |"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "navadhā tuṣṭiḥ | Tats_2.7 |",
          "segment_number": 90,
          "translated_text": "<s>Tuṣṭi</s> (contentment) is ninefold. | Tats_2.7 |"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "aṣṭadhā siddhiḥ | Tats_2.8 |",
          "segment_number": 91,
          "translated_text": "<s>Siddhi</s> (attainment) is eightfold. || Tats_2.8 ||"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "daśa mūlikārthāḥ | Tats_2.9 |",
          "segment_number": 92,
          "translated_text": "The fundamental topics (<s>mūlikārthāḥ</s>) are ten. || Tats_2.9 ||"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "anugrahaḥ sargaḥ | Tats_2.10 |",
          "segment_number": 93,
          "translated_text": "The favorable creation (<s>anugrahasarga</s>). || Tats_2.10 ||"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "caturdaśavidho bhūtasargaḥ | Tats_2.11 |",
          "segment_number": 94,
          "translated_text": "The elemental creation (<s>bhūtasarga</s>) is of fourteen kinds. || Tats_2.11 ||"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "trividho bandhaḥ | Tats_2.12 |",
          "segment_number": 95,
          "translated_text": "<s>Bandha</s> (bondage) is threefold. || Tats_2.12 ||"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "trividho mokṣaḥ | Tats_2.13 |",
          "segment_number": 96,
          "translated_text": "<s>Mokṣa</s> (liberation) is threefold. || Tats_2.13 ||"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "trividhaṃ pramāṇaṃ | Tats_2.14 |",
          "segment_number": 97,
          "translated_text": "<s>Pramāṇa</s> (means of valid knowledge) is threefold. || Tats_2.14 ||"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "trividhaṃ duḥkhaṃ | Tats_2.15 |",
          "segment_number": 98,
          "translated_text": "<s>Duḥkha</s> (suffering) is threefold. || Tats_2.15 ||"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "etatparaṃ yāthātathyaṃ | Tats_2.16 |",
          "segment_number": 99,
          "translated_text": "This is the supreme reality as it truly is (<s>yāthātathya</s>). || Tats_2.16 ||"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "etatjñātvā kṛtakṛtyaḥ syāt | Tats_2.17 |",
          "segment_number": 100,
          "translated_text": "Having known this, one becomes fulfilled (<s>kṛtakṛtya</s>). || Tats_2.17 ||"
        },
        {
          "tag": "l",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "nāsau punaḥ trividhena duḥkhenābhibhūyate nābhibhīyate | Tats_2.18 |",
          "segment_number": 101,
          "translated_text": "He is never again overcome or overpowered by the threefold <s>duḥkha</s> (suffering). || Tats_2.18 ||"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}